Cyrus is sitting at his writing desk, looking at maps of some lands. Having noticed you coming through the door, he puts them aside.
"Mr. Cyrus, do you happen to have the map of Wild Island?" you ask.
"I had it somewhere," he answers, "let's look for it."
You keep searching for quite a long time, in spite of the fact that everyone is trying to help. Alas, the sheet of parchment that is found disappoints you. The map is incomplete and not of much benefit to you.
"Chin up, Henry!" Cyrus consoles you. "Look what I found!"
He holds a massive spyglass in his hands. It consists of two black cylinders, belted by copper rings. The lenses gleam dimly.
"I thought I had lost it long ago!" he smiles. "Well, since we found it thanks to you, take it. It's yours!"
Such a present improves your mood, and now you say goodbye to Cyrus and head to the exit.